---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe29.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Period Between Balance Sheet Date and Approval" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Adjusting Events" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Non-Adjusting Events" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Going Concern Reassessment" },
        { id: "s6", label: "The Approval Date — Marking the End of the Review Period" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Common Examples" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — an Adjusting Event" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — a Non-Adjusting Event" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS 10" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Distinguishing evidence of existing conditions from genuinely new developments</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 29 governs EVENTS occurring AFTER the BALANCE sheet DATE but BEFORE the FINANCIAL statements are APPROVED for ISSUE — DETERMINING whether SUCH events should TRIGGER an ADJUSTMENT to the FINANCIAL statements THEMSELVES, or MERELY a DISCLOSURE — CLOSELY converged with IAS 10 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Period Between Balance Sheet Date and Approval</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies preparing financial statements</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to ALL companies, ADDRESSING events BETWEEN the BALANCE sheet DATE and the DATE financial STATEMENTS are APPROVED for ISSUE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Adjusting Events</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Evidence of conditions that existed at the balance sheet date</div><div class="text-supporting">An ADJUSTING event PROVIDES evidence of CONDITIONS that EXISTED at the BALANCE sheet DATE — the FINANCIAL statements are ADJUSTED to REFLECT this EVIDENCE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Non-Adjusting Events</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Conditions arising after the balance sheet date</div><div class="text-supporting">A NON-ADJUSTING event is INDICATIVE of CONDITIONS that AROSE AFTER the BALANCE sheet DATE — DISCLOSED only, WITH NO adjustment to RECOGNISED amounts.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Going Concern Reassessment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A subsequent event can change the entire basis of preparation</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE a SUBSEQUENT event INDICATES that the GOING CONCERN basis of PREPARATION is NO LONGER appropriate (e.g. a DECISION to LIQUIDATE, arising AFTER the BALANCE sheet DATE), this REQUIRES a FUNDAMENTAL change to the BASIS on WHICH the ENTIRE financial STATEMENTS are PREPARED, RATHER than a NARROW, isolated ADJUSTMENT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Approval Date — Marking the End of the Review Period</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The precise reference point closing the subsequent events window</div><div class="text-supporting">The SUBSEQUENT events REVIEW period RUNS from the BALANCE sheet DATE until the DATE the financial STATEMENTS are APPROVED for ISSUE (TYPICALLY board APPROVAL) — a PRECISE reference POINT determining the FINAL cut-OFF for SUBSEQUENT events ANALYSIS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Common Examples</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Illustrative adjusting and non-adjusting events</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Event type</span><span>Example</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Adjusting</span><span>A CUSTOMER'S bankruptcy CONFIRMING a receivable WAS already impaired at YEAR end</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Non-adjusting</span><span>A FIRE destroying a WAREHOUSE after YEAR end, UNRELATED to conditions EXISTING at year END</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — an Adjusting Event</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reflecting evidence of a pre-existing condition</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Confirming an existing receivable's impairment</div><div class="wk-body">A company's fiscal year ends December 31. On January 20 (before board approval), a major customer with an outstanding receivable at December 31 files for bankruptcy, confirming the customer had already been in serious financial distress at the balance sheet date.</div><div class="wk-answer">This is an ADJUSTING event — the company ADJUSTS its FINANCIAL statements, RECOGNISING an IMPAIRMENT of the RECEIVABLE as AT the BALANCE sheet DATE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Non-Adjusting Event</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Disclosure only, no adjustment to recognised amounts</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A fire destroying a facility after year end</div><div class="wk-body">The same company's warehouse is destroyed by a fire on January 25 — an event with no connection to conditions existing at December 31.</div><div class="wk-answer">This is a NON-ADJUSTING event — the company DISCLOSES the NATURE of the EVENT and, WHERE practicable, an ESTIMATE of its FINANCIAL effect, WITHOUT adjusting the RECOGNISED amounts.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 29 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>The date financial statements were approved for issue</span><span>Nature of material non-adjusting events, and an estimate of their financial effect (or a statement that such an estimate cannot be made)</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Distinguishing adjusting from non-adjusting events</span><span>Whether a subsequent event undermines the going concern basis of preparation</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimated financial effect of a material non-adjusting event, where practicable to determine</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 10</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 29 vs IAS 10</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 29</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 10</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Adjusting/non-adjusting distinction</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Going concern reassessment</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, MIRRORING IAS 10 CLOSELY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every subsequent event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Adjusting event</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised amounts adjusted</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Non-adjusting event</span><span>Notes only</span><span>Disclosed, no adjustment</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 30</span><span>Presentation of Financial Statements — relevant for the going concern basis of preparation this Standard can affect</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Adjusting event</div><div class="glossary-def">A subsequent event providing evidence of conditions existing at the balance sheet date, requiring adjustment to the financial statements.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Approval date</div><div class="glossary-def">The date financial statements are approved for issue, marking the end of the subsequent events review period.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe29 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
